# 1. Reflection

The screen has identified 63 high-confidence hits with strong effect sizes, revealing several key regulatory pathways for IFNG production. Strong negative hits (ZAP70, VAV1, CD3G, CD3D, CD3E, IFNG itself) suggest TCR signaling suppression paradoxically increases IFNG, while positive hits (NFKB2, CBLB, MAP4K1, TSC1) indicate mTOR and NF-κB pathway activation promotes IFNG. The data shows JAK-STAT signaling components are critical (JAK1, JAK3, STAT3 all negative). 

Next steps should focus on: (1) identifying downstream effectors and co-factors of validated pathways, (2) testing genes in chromatin remodeling and transcriptional regulation given KDM1A and BRD4 hits, (3) exploring metabolic regulators (mTOR pathway), and (4) investigating negative feedback mechanisms and cytokine signaling cross-talk.

# 2. Research Plan

